.TITLE "uptime"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Shows how long the system has been running. It reports the __current time__, duration of operation, number of users, and system load averages.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**uptime**
Displays the system uptime and load averages for the last 1, 5, and 15 minutes.
> 

.DIV "SUMMARY"
The load averages displayed by __uptime__ provide a quick way to gauge system performance. A load average higher than the number of CPU cores indicates that the system is experiencing resource contention.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:top** **mac:w**

documentation: __https://ss64.com/osx/uptime.html__
